<node name="CJCA Prep Notes" unique_id="1" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#1688ff" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">CJCA Prep Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Certified Junior Cybersecurity Associate. This file holds your methodology, module notes and exam workspace as a tree of nodes. Pick a node on the left to open it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">The exam
</rich_text>
<rich_text>CJCA is two exams in one: a 5-machine red-team half (user + root flags) and an Elastic SIEM blue-team half (~40 alerts to triage). Work them side by side: your attacks show up as alerts, and the logs hint at attack paths.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Four parts:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 2" foreground="#1688ff">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your methodology, as numbered blank phases that you name and fill in your own way.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 13" foreground="#1688ff">Modules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your notes, one per Academy module, in course order. Your methodology links back to these.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>: your exam workspace, with targets, credentials, findings, flags, SIEM alerts and a log for each day, laid out like the report.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/cjca/tracker/" foreground="#1688ff">CJCA Study Tracker</rich_text>
<rich_text>: the day-by-day study plan for this cert. Check off tasks there as you go.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#d9822b">Read this first
</rich_text>
<rich_text>The report decides whether you pass. One reviewer failed with 60 pages; another passed with 111. Screenshot every step and document negative findings too.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#2f9e44">Do the reporting module
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Do the </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#1688ff">Documentation &amp; Reporting</rich_text>
<rich_text> module from the Penetration Tester path before your exam, even though it isn't in the CJCA path. It shows you how to take notes during an engagement and turn them into the kind of report HTB grades. It's built around the CPTS report, so it won't match the CJCA report one for one. Take the general tips and good habits from it and apply them to the CJCA report template.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">How to use it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. Work through the course in order. As you finish each module, fill in its note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. Build your methodology as you go. Rename each </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">Fill in</rich_text>
<rich_text> phase to a step in your own workflow, and add or delete phases as you need. For a new phase, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Methodology Phase</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Methodology</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Fill each phase with your own checklist, commands and decision points, and link back to the module notes: select some text, pick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Insert › Insert/Edit Link</rich_text>
<rich_text>, choose </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">To Node</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick the note.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>4. Keep one node per tool and one per service under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Services</rich_text>
<rich_text>. For a new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Tool</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Service</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tools &amp; Services</rich_text>
<rich_text>. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 353" foreground="#1688ff">Nmap</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 354" foreground="#1688ff">SMB</rich_text>
<rich_text> are there to start you off. Link them from your module notes and phases so the commands you use most are one click away.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>5. Each module has one child node per Academy section. Expand a module in the tree to see its sections.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>6. On exam day, start at </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> and work from your methodology. The main nodes are in the </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Bookmarks</rich_text>
<rich_text> menu. Click any link to jump to the node behind it.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Command sources</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Get tested commands from these as you go:</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/0bskuru5/HTB-Junior-Cybersecurity_Analyst-Notes" foreground="#1688ff">0bskuru5/HTB-Junior-Cybersecurity_Analyst-Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/sohankanna/CJCA-Study-Notes" foreground="#1688ff">sohankanna/CJCA-Study-Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/mlain24-lab/CJCA_Notes" foreground="#1688ff">mlain24-lab/CJCA_Notes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text>Reporting: </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://docs.sysreptor.com/assets/reports/HTB-CJCA-Report.pdf" foreground="#1688ff">SysReptor HTB-CJCA template</rich_text>
<rich_text> + </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://academy.hackthebox.com/course/preview/documentation--reporting" foreground="#1688ff">Documentation &amp; Reporting module</rich_text>
<rich_text> + </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 314" foreground="#1688ff">M17 - Incident Handling Process</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">Made by</rich_text>
<rich_text> </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://github.com/cnmoseman" foreground="#1688ff">cnmoseman</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://cnmoseman.github.io/htb-study-trackers/" foreground="#1688ff">All HTB Study Trackers</rich_text>
