<codebox char_offset="218" justification="left" frame_width="100" frame_height="74" width_in_pixels="0" syntax_highlighting="sh" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0"># command            # what it does</codebox>
<table char_offset="466" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="240,240,240"><row><cell>e.g. A share anyone can read</cell><cell>e.g. Scripts and config files often hold passwords</cell><cell>e.g. Pull it all down and search it</cell></row><row><cell>What you see</cell><cell>Why it matters</cell><cell>Next step</cell></row></table>
<codebox char_offset="578" justification="left" frame_width="100" frame_height="74" width_in_pixels="0" syntax_highlighting="sh" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0"># command            # what it does</codebox>
</node>
</node>
<node name="Exam" unique_id="355" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="1" foreground="#1688ff" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h1" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Your workspace for exam days: targets, credentials, findings, flags, SIEM alerts and a log for each day. Every table here matches a part of the </rich_text>
<rich_text link="webs https://docs.sysreptor.com/assets/reports/HTB-CJCA-Report.pdf" foreground="#1688ff">official CJCA report template</rich_text>
<rich_text>, so by the end most of the report is already written down.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#e03131">Keep this file private
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Once you start the exam, this file holds exam content. Don't push it to a public GitHub repo or share it, during or after the exam. HTB's terms don't allow it. To lock it with a password, use </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">File › Save As</rich_text>
<rich_text> and pick a </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Password Protected</rich_text>
<rich_text> storage type (</rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">.ctx</rich_text>
<rich_text> or </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">.ctz</rich_text>
<rich_text>).</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Start here</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 356" foreground="#1688ff">01 - Before You Start</rich_text>
<rich_text>: go through the checklist before you start.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 357" foreground="#1688ff">02 - Scope &amp; Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>: copy the scope from the letter of engagement.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>3. Keep a log as you work: </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Log</rich_text>
<rich_text> has one node per exam day, from </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 368" foreground="#1688ff">Day 01</rich_text>
<rich_text> to </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 372" foreground="#1688ff">Day 05</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Targets</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>One node per item under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Targets</rich_text>
<rich_text>. Start with </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 366" foreground="#1688ff">Target 1</rich_text>
<rich_text> and rename it. For each new one, duplicate </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Templates › Target</rich_text>
<rich_text> (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Tree › Duplicate Node</rich_text>
<rich_text>) and drag the copy under </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Targets</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Tracking</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 358" foreground="#1688ff">03 - Network Map</rich_text>
<rich_text>: how the networks connect, and your tunnels.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 359" foreground="#1688ff">04 - Credentials</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every user and secret you find. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Compromised Users</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 360" foreground="#1688ff">05 - SIEM Alerts</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every alert, with your true or false positive verdict. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">SIEM Alert Validation and Analysis</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 361" foreground="#1688ff">06 - Findings</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every vulnerability worth reporting. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Summary of Findings</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 362" foreground="#1688ff">07 - Attack Chain</rich_text>
<rich_text>: the path through the network, step by step.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 363" foreground="#1688ff">08 - Flags</rich_text>
<rich_text>: every flag and where it came from. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Flags Discovered</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 364" foreground="#1688ff">09 - Cleanup</rich_text>
<rich_text>: everything you changed on a host. Report: </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Changes/Host Cleanup</rich_text>
<rich_text>.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<encoded_png char_offset="0" justification="left" link=""></encoded_png>
<node name="01 - Before You Start" unique_id="356" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Setup</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>VPN connects and you can reach the first target</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Screenshot tool ready (Flameshot or similar). Paste each screenshot straight into the host's node with </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">Ctrl+V</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Screenshot names picked, like </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">web01-03-shell.png</rich_text>
<rich_text> (item, step, what it shows), so you can find each one when you write the report</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Terminal logging on (</rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">tmux</rich_text>
<rich_text> logging or </rich_text>
<rich_text family="monospace" foreground="#1688ff">script</rich_text>
<rich_text>) so you keep every command and its output</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Report started from the HTB CJCA template in SysReptor</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>SIEM alert list copied from the report template in the exam lab</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Autosave and backups on: </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">File › Preferences › Miscellaneous</rich_text>
<rich_text>, tick </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Autosave Every x Minutes</rich_text>
<rich_text> and </rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Create a Backup Copy Before Saving</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>A copy of this file kept somewhere private. Only open it in one CherryTree window at a time, or you can lose changes</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Read</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Letter of engagement read twice, scope copied into </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 357" foreground="#1688ff">02 - Scope &amp; Rules</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Exam start time, end time and report deadline written down</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>What counts as a flag and how to submit it</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Plan</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Rough plan for each day, with real breaks</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text>Sleep plan. Long exams are lost to fatigue more often than to missing skills.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Wordlists and tools ready on your attack box</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
</node>
<node name="02 - Scope &amp; Rules" unique_id="357" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">In Scope Assets</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">copy these from the letter of engagement; the report has the same table</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Out of Scope</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. A host the letter says not to touch</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Rules of Engagement</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>• </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. No denial of service</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Timeline</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="88" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="191,236"><row><cell>e.g. 10.129.x.x</cell><cell>e.g. External web server</cell></row><row><cell>Host/URL/IP Address</cell><cell>Description</cell></row></table>
<table char_offset="206" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="110,240"><row><cell>Exam start</cell><cell>e.g. 2026-11-01 09:00 UTC</cell></row><row><cell>Exam end</cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>Report due</cell><cell></cell></row><row><cell>Item</cell><cell>Date and time</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="03 - Network Map" unique_id="358" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Map</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>Sketch how the networks connect in the box below, or paste a screenshot of a diagram (</rich_text>
<rich_text weight="heavy">Insert › Insert Image</rich_text>
<rich_text>).</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Tunnels</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Subnets</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<codebox char_offset="114" justification="left" frame_width="100" frame_height="74" width_in_pixels="0" syntax_highlighting="text" highlight_brackets="1" show_line_numbers="0">[attack box] --&gt; [external host] --&gt; [internal subnet] --&gt; [DC]</codebox>
<table char_offset="126" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="133,206,203,206,149"><row><cell>e.g. Attack box</cell><cell>e.g. An internal subnet via a foothold host</cell><cell>e.g. Ligolo-ng or chisel</cell><cell>e.g. (the command you ran)</cell><cell>e.g. a local port</cell></row><row><cell>From</cell><cell>To</cell><cell>Tool</cell><cell>Command</cell><cell>Local port</cell></row></table>
<table char_offset="137" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="218,218,240"><row><cell>e.g. an internal range</cell><cell>e.g. the foothold host</cell><cell>e.g. the hosts you discover there</cell></row><row><cell>Subnet</cell><cell>Reached from</cell><cell>Hosts found</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="04 - Credentials" unique_id="359" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">In the report
</rich_text>
<rich_text>The Username, Type, Method and Notes columns become the </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Compromised Users</rich_text>
<rich_text> table.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">Type: password, NTLM hash, Kerberos ticket, SSH key, other. Link the host note in Found on.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">To Try</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">creds you haven't tested everywhere yet</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>☐ </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Reuse a found password across the other hosts</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="96" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="126,121,95,139,139,139,137"><row><cell>e.g. a service account</cell><cell>e.g. password or hash</cell><cell>e.g. (the value)</cell><cell>e.g. the host you found it on</cell><cell>e.g. where it was exposed</cell><cell>e.g. the host it works on</cell><cell>e.g. its privilege there</cell></row><row><cell>Username</cell><cell>Type</cell><cell>Secret</cell><cell>Found on</cell><cell>Method</cell><cell>Works on</cell><cell>Notes</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="05 - SIEM Alerts" unique_id="360" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>Work the blue-team half here. Your own attacks from the red-team half show up as alerts, so cross-check them.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">Verdict: true positive (real malicious activity) or false positive (benign activity flagged by mistake).</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="111" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="60,147,185,140,185,185"><row><cell>e.g. 1</cell><cell>e.g. the alert name</cell><cell>e.g. the host it fired on</cell><cell>e.g. when it fired</cell><cell>e.g. true or false positive</cell><cell>e.g. the log that proves it</cell></row><row><cell>No.</cell><cell>Alert Name</cell><cell>Host</cell><cell>Timestamp</cell><cell>Verdict</cell><cell>Evidence</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="06 - Findings" unique_id="361" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>Write every finding here as you go, then write each one up properly in the report. A finding can be on the attack path or standalone.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Each finding needs</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>In the report, every finding has: a severity (High, Medium or Low), steps to reproduce, collected evidence and remediation.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Severity</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text foreground="#8a8d96">────────────────────────────────────────
</rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 355" foreground="#1688ff">Exam</rich_text>
<rich_text> · </rich_text>
<rich_text link="node 1" foreground="#1688ff">Home</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<table char_offset="135" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="60,161,148,178,178,178"><row><cell>e.g. 1</cell><cell>e.g. the vulnerability</cell><cell>e.g. the host or app</cell><cell>e.g. High, Medium, Low or Info</cell><cell>e.g. yes once the screenshot is saved</cell><cell>e.g. yes once it's written up</cell></row><row><cell>#</cell><cell>Finding</cell><cell>Where</cell><cell>Severity</cell><cell>Evidence ready</cell><cell>In report</cell></row></table>
<table char_offset="291" justification="left" col_min="60" col_max="240" is_light="0" col_widths="92,164"><row><cell>Critical</cell><cell>9.0 to 10.0</cell></row><row><cell>High</cell><cell>7.0 to 8.9</cell></row><row><cell>Medium</cell><cell>4.0 to 6.9</cell></row><row><cell>Low</cell><cell>0.1 to 3.9</cell></row><row><cell>Info</cell><cell>0.0</cell></row><row><cell>Rating</cell><cell>CVSS score range</cell></row></table>
</node>
<node name="07 - Attack Chain" unique_id="362" master_id="0" prog_lang="custom-colors" tags="cjca exam" readonly="0" nosearch_me="0" nosearch_ch="0" custom_icon_id="0" is_bold="0" foreground="" ts_creation="1792540800" ts_lastsave="1792540800">
<rich_text>The path from first foothold to full compromise. Feeds the report's </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">Internal Network Compromise Walkthrough</rich_text>
<rich_text>. Only the steps on the path go here; everything else stays a standalone finding.</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">High-Level Steps</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Got a foothold on the external host through a web vulnerability</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>2. </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. Reused a found credential to reach an internal host</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Access Gained</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">one row per step above, so you can see where each jump came from</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text scale="h2" weight="heavy" foreground="#1688ff">Detailed Steps</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic" foreground="#8a8d96">reproduction steps, with links to the host notes and the commands you ran</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>1. </rich_text>
<rich_text style="italic">e.g. On the external host, exploited the upload form, then confirmed code execution</rich_text>
<rich_text>
</rich_text>
<rich_text>
